Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["KnoodleProve", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"0cb3e8cb-1975-4d0a-8e1b-136d64cac096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"c5ca1354-4e7d-4d1c-9d95-791a9c88296b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"KnoodleProve", "[", 
   StyleBox["trace", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0c49887f-df9b-4f6a-8337-01b06c52d08b"],
 "\[LineSeparator]checks the claims of a move trace, and says whether it \
proves its input an unlink."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"58fd0dd9-7c5c-42fd-afa7-f7e8b0dec46d"],

Cell["\<\
A move trace is the record a simplifier writes of the moves it made on a knot \
or link diagram: the diagram it started from and, for each move, the move and \
the diagram it left. The format is Knoodle's docs/move-descriptor.md. Nothing \
in Knoodle writes a trace yet; the traces bundled with this paclet were \
recorded by the simplifier of the middlestrands project, which is built on \
Knoodle.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"62bf10d8-c93d-4662-853f-2f399cb56f88"],

Cell["\<\
trace is File[path], a path to a trace file, or the trace's text as a string.\
\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"abda3bd6-25ee-4cac-bebb-3ac12bcce733"],

Cell["\<\
KnoodleProve runs Knoodle's knoodleprove, which checks every claim in the \
trace that does not depend on a drawing: that each move is well formed \
against its diagram, that it produces the next record's diagram, that the \
pieces it frees are the ones the trace names, and that a middle pass's \
feasibility witness holds. Pass, middle-pass, curl-removal (r1) and redraw \
moves are checked. A move of any other kind is reported as UNCHECKED, never \
skipped. A record marked #candidate is a move the simplifier evaluated but \
did not make: its claims are checked, but it is not part of the proof.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ac1c81d3-17a3-4568-a0db-ae46ea9b4a22"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an Association. \"Verdict\" is \"VERIFIED\" when every claim \
checked out, \"MISMATCH\" when some claim is false, and \"UNCHECKED\" when \
none is false but some could not be checked. \"Unlink\" is True when the \
trace ends at the empty diagram and that, with every move sound and every \
component freed exactly once, proves its input an unlink: for a knot, the \
unknot. \"Claims\" lists the claims in order, one Association each, with keys \
\"Step\" (the record's number, or All for a claim about the whole trace), \
\"Claim\", \"Verdict\" and \"Detail\". A line that only reports, such as \
which components a move freed, has \"Verdict\" -> None.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c5ef0e96-b71d-4c46-837b-4ca0f003645c"],

Cell["\<\
A false claim is an answer, not a failure: the result says \"MISMATCH\", and \
the claim's \"Detail\" says what is wrong. A trace that knoodleprove cannot \
read gives $Failed with a KnoodleProve::knoodletool message quoting its error.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"65b42f88-35e6-4367-ab7b-0cde884e365f"],

Cell["\<\
The claims that do depend on a drawing (that the pictures of a move show the \
right diagrams) belong to knoodledraw --trace --verify, which this paclet \
does not wrap.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a36b5799-6b44-46a2-9c0b-01b82bbdb4cc"],

Cell["The following options can be given:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b3328522-4738-481b-a499-3ccc18031e8e"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "47068e4d-cb87-470e-a983-baa97f0e6748"], "\"\<CheckExterior\>\"", 
    "False", Cell["\<\
also check each record's '#view' claim: that its outside face is the image of \
the previous record's across the move\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c4fc86c4-9375-47d4-a42e-d76e860a47cf"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"5f20943c-b964-45fa-9e34-\
6f5b80fb10f5"]
}, Open  ]],

